  "body": "The four T16 owner maps admitted in the PR1047 review improve a particular\ncertified exponent, but their joint repacks need not improve every concave\ncost. This audit reconstructs all 276,480 roles and proves that five of the\nsix map pairs are incomparable by majorization. Only PR1028 -> PR1031 has\nthe universal concave ordering.\n\nFor the selected PR1031 -> PR1042 change, exact rational bounds show that\n`phi_b(r)=73^b*r^(1-b)-r` decreases at b=1/2 but increases at b=3/4. This\nconcrete reversal bounds the applicability of the inherited greedy exchange\nproof; it does not contradict the reviewed selected small-exponent result\nor change kappa. The source maps, classical majorization argument and T16\nconstruction are fully credited.\n\nValidation: source-pinned whole-role reconstruction; an independent dense-bin,\nsorted-prefix and Fraction-bisection cross-check; eight mathematical checks,\nsix package rejections and a spaced-path relocation replay. All three\nstandard-library commands pass under isolated optimized Python. Physical\ncharts, native semantics, invoices and all-size admission remain upstream\nobligations rather than claims of this narrow audit.\n\nFixed base: ba82555c64e1879e4b7decce28186f208fcb8262, selected PR1042.\nPrepared by @woklerx with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance; Apache-2.0.\n",
